<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Rains delay Texas harvest.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Rains delay Texas harvest.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rainy weather has delayed harvest activity around Fort Worth, Texas, but grain dealers said Friday they expected the hard red winter wheat harvest to pick up again by the middle of next week.</p>
<p>&quot;The harvest in Fort Worth has been slow to start. We have seen some bushels come in from there, but it's not enough to get a good sense of the crop quality,&quot; a south central Kansas dealer said. &quot;I think the real crunch will begin next week.&quot;</p>
<p>Meanwhile, spot cash basis bids at terminals in the Gulf and in the country were higher as demand stayed strong and as the wheat harvest was delayed.</p>
<p>Merchandisers said wheat had traded Thursday at the Gulf at 88 cents over the KCBT July contract.  </p>
